diff --git a/doc/pod/pullnews.pod b/doc/pod/pullnews.pod
index 9617a61..f79105d 100644
--- a/doc/pod/pullnews.pod
+++ b/doc/pod/pullnews.pod
@@ -332,13 +332,22 @@ duplicate work the next time it runs.
 
 The full syntax is:
 
-    <host>[:<port>][_<tlsmode>] [<username> <password>]
+    <host>[:<port>][_<tlsmode>] [<username> <password-specification>]
         <group> [<time> <high>]
         <group> [<time> <high>]
 
 where the <host> line must not have leading whitespace and the <group>
 lines must.
 
+The password specification is normally a literal password.  Prefix it with
+C<@> to read the password from a file instead.  A specification of the form
+C<@credential:I<name>> reads I<name> below the directory named by the
+C<CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY> environment variable, as used by systemd service
+credentials.  Prefix a literal password that begins with C<@> with another
+C<@>.  File-based passwords must contain exactly one non-empty line; the final
+line ending is removed.  Password references, rather than their resolved
+contents, are preserved when B<pullnews> updates the configuration file.
+
 A typical configuration file would be:
 
     # Format: group date high
